  "id": "ventilation",
  "term": "ventilation",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, ventilation refers to increased breathing, often done in a group breathwork setting and sometimes sustained long enough to change body chemistry. Prolonged increased breathing can lower carbon dioxide, alter nervous system activity, and affect perception, cognition, and mental well-being.",
